  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">REACH - Capital Element ICF IWSP - To produce robust and accessible evidence for policy decision-makers in Africa and South Asia, on how to ensure sustainable delivery of water services at scale, and better understand the cost benefits and trade</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity REACH - Capital Element ICF IWSP - To produce robust and accessible evidence for policy decision-makers in Africa and South Asia, on how to ensure sustainable delivery of water services at scale, and better understand the cost benefits and trade is a component of REACH: Improving water security for poor people reported by FCDO with a funding type of 104 - Procurement of Services and a budget of &#xA3;7,042,483. This project benefits Africa, regional. It works in the following sector(s): Environmental research, Research/scientific institutions, Water resources conservation (including data collection), Water sector policy and administrative management, River basins development.</narrative>
  </description>
